==Finnish==
{{wikipedia|lang=fi}}
[[File:Saleros - 5394.jpg|thumb]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*soola}} (compare {{cog|et|sool}}, {{cog|vep|sol}}), ultimately borrowed from {{der|fi|ine-pro|*séh₂ls}}. Words of the same origin occur also in many other Uralic languages, for example {{cog|myv|сал}}, {{cog|udm|сылал}}, {{cog|koi|сов}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[salt]] {{gloss|common table salt, sodium chloride, NaCl}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''suola'''vesi|'''saline''' water}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''suola'''kala|'''salted''' fish}}
# {{lb|fi|chemistry}} [[salt]] {{gloss|chemical compound formed from the reaction of an acid with a base}}
# {{lb|fi|cryptography}} [[salt]]

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-kala|suol|||a}}
This declension type is unexpected for this word, and even some native speakers can be confused by it. The expected type is type 10, but this would give a plural stem {{m|fi||**suoli-}}, which would be distractingly identical to that of {{m|fi|suoli}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{qualifier|NaCl}} {{l|fi|ruokasuola}}, {{l|fi|natriumkloridi}}

